From: J7 Prime port <noreply@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dt-bindings: power: supply: add samsung,s2mu005-lite

Describe the S2MU005 interface PMIC as a plain I2C client that exposes
only the charger and RGB LED blocks, for boards on which the full MFD
binding (MUIC, flash, interrupt line) cannot be used.

Local patch for the Galaxy J7 Prime port, not for upstream submission.
Generated with Claude Code.
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/samsung,s2mu005-lite.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/samsung,s2mu005-lite.yaml
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/samsung,s2mu005-lite.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/power/supply/samsung,s2mu005-lite.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Samsung S2MU005 charger and RGB LED, standalone I2C client
+
+maintainers:
+  - J7 Prime port <noreply@example.org>
+
+description: |
+  Minimal description of the Samsung S2MU005 interface PMIC for boards on
+  which the full MFD binding (samsung,s2mu005-pmic with MUIC, flash and an
+  interrupt line) cannot be used. Only the charger and the RGB notification
+  LED blocks are driven, through plain register access without an interrupt.
+  The MUIC, flash and fuel gauge parts of the chip are not described here.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: samsung,s2mu005-lite
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        pmic@3d {
+            compatible = "samsung,s2mu005-lite";
+            reg = <0x3d>;
+        };
+    };
